RISC-V SYNTHESIS AND PRE-LAYOUT STA
RTL checkout: ba699982a1439b8ddbb70346c1edaa4cd8e979b6
Design top: riscv_core
Sources: eight entries in Synthesis/setup/riscv_core.filelist
Reference run: local Yosys / ABC / OpenSTA
Library: sky130_fd_sc_hs__ss_100C_1v60, slow process, 1.60 V, 100 C
SDC: Synthesis/validation/riscv_core_10ns.sdc, core_clk, 10 ns, ideal clock
Scope: flattened standard-cell mapping and single-corner pre-layout STA.
       No placed/routed parasitics, clock tree, or fast-corner hold analysis.

RESULTS
                                   Initial mapping       Buffered and sized
Mapped cells                               28,678                   32,626
Mapped DFFs                                 8,524                    8,524
Liberty cell area (um^2)              417,962.419              449,428.522
Setup WNS (ns)                           -205.492                   -2.927
Setup TNS (ns)                         -1,311,812.000          -23,546.281
Worst reported hold (ns)                   +0.420                   +0.420
Post-map structural problems                    0                        0
RTL smoke test                              PASS                     PASS
Zero-delay gate smoke test                  PASS                     PASS

Both smoke tests produced io_out = 0x00005555 at 55 ns. Gate simulation
used functional models derived from the same Liberty. A zero-delay smoke
test verifies the boot sequence and does not exercise the reported delays.
The optimized map failed the 10 ns setup target. Its worst reported path
implies approximately 12.927 ns for zero setup slack in this pre-layout
model, before changes to constraints or parasitics.

Worst setup path in the optimized run:
  _56672_/Q (u_pc.pc[16]) -> _53019_/D (u_dmem.mem[23][11])
  Arrival: 12.645 ns. Required: 9.718 ns. Slack: -2.927 ns.
  Clock path: ideal. The endpoint is a mapped data-memory flop.

FLOW DIAGNOSTICS AND ACTIONS

Synth-001 | Missing testbench path | FIXED
Baseline failed with Errno 2 on RiscV-32bit/RiscV-32bit.srcs/sim_1/new/tb_riscv_core.v.
Fix: Point the runner to the existing sources_1/new/tb_riscv_core.v. The
testbench and FPGA wrapper are only used as simulation inputs.

Synth-002 | Liberty generation and OpenSTA compatibility | FIXED
The upstream generator needed dataclasses-json. Its module launcher also
stopped on two internal TimingType doctest failures in this environment.
Fix: Install the dependency and invoke the generator's main function.
OpenSTA 2.0.17 then emitted:
  Warning: cells.lib, line 19 default_operating_condition max_ind not found.
Fix: Move the default_operating_conditions declaration below the matching
operating_conditions group in a run-local copy. The corner name, PVT and
all timing tables are preserved. The warning disappeared. The setup slack
was identical with the original and reordered Liberty.

Synth-003 | Sequential mapping warnings | REVIEWED
Yosys 0.23 reported 26 unique warnings (234 total), all for unsupported
pin expressions in scan or enable flop definitions. Examples:
  'D&!SCE|SCD&SCE' in sky130_fd_sc_hs__sdfbbn_1
  'D&DE|IQ&!DE' in sky130_fd_sc_hs__edfxtp_1
  'D&DE&!SCE|IQ&!DE&!SCE|SCD&SCE' in sky130_fd_sc_hs__sedfxtp_1
ABC also reports excluding sequential, tri-state, and non-logic cells
from combinational mapping. dfflibmap mapped 8,524 positive-edge flops
to sky130_fd_sc_hs__dfxtp_1. The runner loads the target cell interfaces,
checks all references, and fails on unmapped cells or structural errors.
Action for DFT: Qualify scan-cell mappings before scan insertion.

Synth-004 | High fanout in first mapping | FIXED IN FLOW
The initial worst path contained a minimum-drive nor2b_1 driving 2,052
loads (5.937 pF). OpenSTA reported 89.976 ns across that arc, with
125.980 ns output slew, well beyond the library's 1 ns default limit.
Fix: Feed ABC a dummy buf_4 driver and 5 fF load through -constr to
enable buffering and sizing. Keep the 10,000 ps mapping target and 10 ns
STA clock. This recovered 202.565 ns of setup slack with the same RTL.
The driver and load apply to ABC's extracted network and are illustrative.

Synth-005 | Missing I/O constraints | DUMMY COVERAGE CHECKED
The clock-only baseline reports no input delay for reset and no output
delay for 132 bits. Those 132 output bits are reported as unconstrained.
Fix for coverage testing: The optional riscv_core_10ns_io_example.sdc
assigns illustrative min/max reset and output delays and transition/load.
The rerun removed the missing-delay warnings. The remaining 11 endpoints
are dbg_instr bits driven by constants from the built-in ROM. Verified
their constant assignments in the mapped netlist. The worst setup path
with these provisional budgets is reset to dbg_zero, slack -5.110 ns.
The I/O example has worst reported hold +0.331 ns at the same slow corner.
Use actual reset timing and debug/output budgets before evaluating closure.

Synth-006 | Standalone cell simulation models | FIXED FOR SMOKE CHECK
Raw upstream functional wrappers reference helper modules absent from the
cell checkout. The direct simulation compile failed on a missing
u_vpwr_vgnd include, followed by unresolved cell modules.
Fix: Generate zero-delay functional Verilog from the run's Liberty via
Yosys read_liberty, retain the cell types present in the mapped netlist,
and compile those models with the netlist and existing testbench. The
optimized netlist passed the smoke check. Obtain assembled PDK simulation
models and back-annotated delays for a timing simulation.

RTL CHANGES FOR REVIEW ONLY
No design RTL or testbench changes were made.
1. data_mem.v:13-29. The 256 x 32 array has a full synchronous reset and
   asynchronous read. It maps to flops and a large mux/enable network in
   this flow. If area or 10 ns timing is a requirement, evaluate a
   characterized memory macro. Preserve reset-visible zero behavior
   with valid bits or a documented initialization sequence if the macro
   cannot reset its contents. Account for read latency and MMIO behavior.
2. riscv_core.v:16-136. If 10 ns still fails after placement-aware timing
   optimization, evaluate a register boundary between fetch/decode and
   the execute/memory path. Preserve PC redirects and store ordering, and
   verify the added cycle with the testbench and formal properties.

REPRODUCTION
Tools: Yosys 0.23 (7ce5011c24b), ABC 1.01, OpenSTA 2.0.17,
       Icarus Verilog 12.0.
SkyWater HS cell data: google/skywater-pdk-libs-sky130_fd_sc_hs
  revision 1d051f49bfe4e2fe9108d702a8bc2e9c081005a4
SkyWater Liberty generator: google/skywater-pdk
  revision 7198cf647113f56041e02abf3eb623692820c5e1
Guide: https://lab.chipverify.com/guide (High Speed, Slow)
Generate the raw .lib from the two SkyWater checkouts with dataclasses-json
0.6.7 and the generator's Python package on PYTHONPATH:
  python3 -c 'from skywater_pdk.liberty import main; raise SystemExit(main())' \
    /path/to/hs ss_100C_1v60 -o /path/to/output
For OpenSTA 2.0.17, move the single line
  default_operating_conditions : "max_ind";
below the closing brace of the operating_conditions ("max_ind") group.
Raw Liberty SHA-256:
  152939238a3a2f69cef497df0ccb98e77479ab00da5f820c6e0b9c532bb25204
Reordered Liberty SHA-256:
  577d56827d3230109df840f19eff5cf8476bd431555ae51a5cbd90759121f15c
Mapped netlist SHA-256:
  a257c733f5d863ef58b2e1b9cd60dd1e3d7800363861d73dd27048a9d6483e62

Run from the repository root with the tools on PATH:
  python3 Synthesis/validation/run_riscv_baseline.py \
    --liberty /path/to/sky130_fd_sc_hs__ss_100C_1v60.lib \
    --abc-constraints Synthesis/compile/sky130_hs_abc.constr \
    --out build/riscv_hs_ss
Omit --abc-constraints to reproduce the initial mapping. The runner writes
the full simulation, synthesis and STA logs, replay scripts, netlist and
RTL waveform. For the optional I/O coverage check, use the generated STA
script with read_sdc pointing to riscv_core_10ns_io_example.sdc and rerun
STA on the optimized netlist.
